    "body": "Panic texts on origin/main fd64cc2f5 (debug, `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --test multiaxis --test multiaxis_avoid --test multiaxis_rough`):\n\n- `multiaxis.rs:180` `rapids_hold_the_pose_they_inherit`:\n  `assertion left == right failed: a rapid changed the pose it inherited: Move { kind: Rapid, from: (0, 0, 20), to: (4.919, -8.452, 20), axis: Some([0.0, 0.0, 1.0]) }` - left `Some([0.0, 0.0, 1.0])`, right `None`.\n- `multiaxis_avoid.rs:176` `dodging_never_moves_the_ball`:\n  `a rapid changed the pose it inherited` - left `Some([0.0, 0.0, 1.0])`, right `None`.\n- `multiaxis_rough.rs:161` `rapids_and_floors_hold_no_pose_and_flanks_do`:\n  `a rapid changed the pose it inherited` - left `Some([0.0, 0.0, 1.0])`, right `None`.\n\nAll three fail at the same line type: the first opening rapid at the clearance. Each test starts its \"inherited pose\" memory at `None`. The #3300 stamp rule makes the opening rapid of a path that leans state the upright Z column, the home that the stamp itself holds (`held = UP`). The rapid states the pose it inherits from the home, not a new angle. No tilted pose is involved: the failing move is before the first lean. Next: the decision for each test.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
